# @foodello/intercom — Contributor Rules

## What This Is

A Capacitor plugin that bridges the Intercom iOS SDK, Intercom Android SDK, and `@intercom/messenger-js-sdk` (web) to a unified TypeScript API. It is published as `@foodello/intercom` on npm.

The plugin major version tracks Capacitor major (plugin v8 = Capacitor v8). Breaking changes only ship with a new Capacitor major version.

## Repository Layout

```
src/
  definitions.ts    Public API — TypeScript interfaces, enums, JSDoc. Source of truth.
  index.ts          registerPlugin() entry point
  web.ts            Web implementation (uses @intercom/messenger-js-sdk)
ios/Plugin/
  IntercomPlugin.swift    iOS native (CAPPlugin subclass)
android/src/main/java/com/getcapacitor/community/intercom/
  IntercomPlugin.java     Android native (Plugin subclass, Java 21)
dist/               Generated — never edit
FoodelloIntercom.podspec  CocoaPods spec
```

## Source of Truth

`src/definitions.ts` drives:
- TypeScript types consumed by end users
- Auto-generated API docs in `README.md` (between `<docgen-index>` and `<docgen-api>` tags)
- `dist/docs.json`

**Never edit `<docgen-index>` or `<docgen-api>` sections in README.md directly.**
Update JSDoc in `src/definitions.ts`, then run `npm run docgen` or `npm run build`.

## Build & Verify

```bash
npm run build        # tsc + rollup + docgen
npm run verify       # iOS + Android + Web (run before every commit)
npm run fmt          # ESLint + Prettier + SwiftLint (auto-fix)
npm run lint         # check only
npm run verify:web   # fast — just TypeScript + rollup
```

## iOS Rules

- All Intercom and UIKit calls must be on `DispatchQueue.main.async`.
- Events fire via `notifyListeners("eventName", data: [...])`.
- Both **CocoaPods** (`FoodelloIntercom.podspec`) and **Swift Package Manager** must keep working.
- `setupIntercom()` is called from `load()` (static keys) or `loadWithKeys()` (dynamic keys).
- Identity verification: `setUserHash(hmac:)` must be called **before** `loginIdentifiedUser`. If the order is wrong, Intercom silently degrades to unverified — document this clearly in any PR touching auth.
- `IntercomSpace` on iOS: `.home`, `.messages`, `.helpCenter`, `.tickets` — `news` and `tasks` are web-only; guard with `call.reject` if received.
- `IntercomContent` on iOS: `carousel`, `survey`, `article`, `conversation` — other variants are web-only.

## Android Rules

- Java **21** only. No Java 8 lambdas, no records, no newer language features.
- All UI calls must run on `bridge.getActivity().runOnUiThread(_:)`.
- Push handled via `IntercomPushClient`.
- `handleOnStart()` calls `setupIntercom()` and `Intercom.client().handlePushMessage()` — do not remove this.

## Web Rules

- `IntercomWeb` extends `WebPlugin` from `@capacitor/core`.
- State is maintained in a local `State` object (booted, config, initialized, isVisible, unreadCount, unreadListenerAttached).
- Methods not supported on web (`loginIdentifiedUser`, `loginUnidentifiedUser`, `receivePush`, `sendPushTokenToIntercom`, `loadWithKeys`) must throw `this.unimplemented('Not implemented on web.')`.
- `load(config)` boots the SDK and wires show/hide/userEmailSupplied listeners.
- Unread count listener is managed internally via `onUnreadCountChange`.

## Common Pitfalls

| Pitfall | Why it matters |
|---|---|
| `setUserHash` called after `loginIdentifiedUser` | Identity verification silently degrades — always call before login |
| `setupUnreadConversationListener()` not called before `addListener('updateUnreadCount', ...)` | Events never fire on native |
| Forgetting `removeUnreadConversationListener()` | Duplicate events from stale `NotificationCenter` observers |
| Editing `dist/` | Fully regenerated on build — changes are lost |
| `CompanyOption.companyId` missing on native | Required for company association; `name` is required on web |
| Breaking CocoaPods or SPM | Users depend on both — verify both before merging |
| `Carousel`, `receivePush` on web | These are native-only; throw `unimplemented` |

## PR Checklist

- [ ] `npm run verify` passes (all three platforms)
- [ ] `npm run fmt` run (no lint/format errors)
- [ ] `src/definitions.ts` updated if public API changed
- [ ] `README.md` API sections regenerated via `npm run docgen`
- [ ] No breaking changes (unless aligned with a new Capacitor major)
- [ ] Both CocoaPods and SPM remain functional if iOS files changed
